      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-327450",
      ":question/problem": "In a climate-controlled lab, a heated ceramic tile was placed on a counter in a room that maintained a constant temperature of $60^{\u2218}F$. At $t = 0$ minutes, the tile\u2019s temperature was $180^{\u2218}F$. After $5$ minutes, its temperature had dropped to $150^{\u2218}F$, and after $10$ minutes, it was $127.5^{\u2218}F$. The tile continued to cool over time.\n\nWhich of the following functions best models the temperature $T(t)$ in degrees Fahrenheit of the tile $t$ minutes after it was placed on the counter?"
